# Apple clang 26 accepts a fourth, string argument to __ptrauth; upstream clang,
# including the one scripts/linux/setup-toolchain.py builds, stops at "must take
# between 1 and 3 arguments". The only use is ucred.cr_label, which no userland
# object reads, so non-Apple compilers keep the type discriminator.
ptrauth-string-discriminator.patch
# ArmCpu's weak_import sleep hook has no definition in any component; ld64-port
# rejects the unresolved weak data symbol when the archive joins the kernel link.
armcpu-sleep-hook.patch
# The reference kernel compiles the vendored corecrypto assembler, which only
# used the portable v0.4s spelling for Apple clang; upstream clang rejects the
# q-register form, so a clean build stops there.
corecrypto-vector-crypto.patch
# Stage 0 has no serial hardware and no display driver, so the panel is the only
# output: three bars from start.s while the MMU is off, then the stock video
# console in text mode once arm_vm_init has run.
f2-start-breadcrumbs.patch
ios27-panel-console.patch
# The firmware leaves the EL1 physical-timer bank unavailable: the CNTP_CTL_EL0
# write at fiq_context_init faults, and XNU reports it as an undefined kernel
# instruction. The iOS 16.6.1 line carries the same fix for this board.
k60-virtual-timer.patch
# 8x16 glyphs on a 1440x3200 panel cannot be read from a photograph, and the
# panic text is the only evidence Stage 0 produces. k60_fontscale=3 makes the
# console 60x66 cells of 24x48 pixels; without the argument every path is the
# stock one.
k60-console-font-scale.patch
